    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d45">

                <pb facs="0179" n="94" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg94"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123D322/59b</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Director of the Consular Service of the Department
                        of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Carr</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to Consul William Dawson</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-10-06"><hi rendition="#italic">October 6,
                        1919</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: You are hereby designated as American
                    Commissioner at Dantzig, and you are instructed to proceed to Dantzig and assume
                    your duties as early as possible.</p>
                <p>Mr. Albert Halstead, Jr., who is now in the United States, has been offered the
                    position of clerk at Dantzig and has been instructed to arrange to proceed with
                    you.</p>
                <p>You are authorized to purchase necessary furniture and furnishings for the
                    opening of the office, keeping these expenditures as low as practicable, and not
                    exceeding a total of $500. You will, as early as practicable after your arrival
                    at your post, submit an itemized estimate of the expenses of conducting the
                    office.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilbur J. Carr</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
